{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"7fcdc72f4709ecac4599102188f9582e61c14b0abaee31a18dc1cdf6caf1da44","digest":{"component_or_area":"ticket close path / store compaction","key_entities":["src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","src/rebar/_commands/compact_txn.py","_compact_on_close","compact_txn._compact_locked",".ticket-write.lock.d","src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py","tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_does_not_compact_barbet.py","docs/concurrency.md"],"problem_keywords":["write lock contention","compaction","ticket close","lock hold duration","concurrent writes"],"propositions":["Closing a ticket invokes _compact_on_close, which holds the store write lock for minutes (measured 13m53s in one case) while folding events, reducing snapshots, and committing to git","The write lock hold blocks concurrent agents from acquiring it, causing writes to time out and be lost","Compaction is optional housekeeping and not a correctness requirement; event logs remain valid unfolded and are replayed correctly by the reducer","Removing _compact_on_close from the close path restores close-induced lock holds to short bursts while leaving the standalone rebar compact command and out-of-band compaction intact","No test in the codebase relied on compact-on-close as a side effect except test_canonical_event_bytes.py, which was decoupled by making its compaction explicit"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b2b5c498-2f67-4ae3-bafc-eca40294bec2","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1786601142505074286,"uuid":"ba8e91f3-1906-489e-80a5-ff9e1d5f6e1c"}